the knowledge base module_3_examples includes:

the text of the source program is at "sources/module-3-examples.l4".

the age category for an age N is a text if
    N < 18
    and the text is equal to "minor"
    otherwise the text is equal to "adult".

the letter grade for a score S is a text if
    S >= 90
    and the text is equal to "A"
    otherwise S >= 80
    and the text is equal to "B"
    otherwise S >= 70
    and the text is equal to "C"
    otherwise S >= 60
    and the text is equal to "D"
    otherwise the text is equal to "F".

the amount category for an amount N is a text if
    N < 100
    and the text is equal to "small"
    otherwise N < 1000
    and the text is equal to "medium"
    otherwise the text is equal to "large".

the person can vote for an age N with a boolean if
    N >= 18
    and true is equal to the boolean.

the transaction needs review for an amount N with a boolean if
    N > 10000
    or true is equal to the boolean.

the person is a minor for an age N if
    it is not the case that N >= 18.

all a numbers are positive if
    for all cases in which
        a number N is in the numbers
        it is the case that
            N > 0.

some number is negative for a numbers if
    a number N is in the numbers
    and N < 0.

the numbers above threshold for a numbers with a threshold T is a list L if
    L is the list of each N such that
        a number N is in the numbers
        and N > T.

the describe the list for an items is a text if
    [] is equal to the items
    and the text is equal to "no items"
    otherwise prolog (the items=[T|N])
    and [] is equal to N
    and the text is equal to "one item"
    otherwise prolog (the items=[M|K])
    and the text is equal to "multiple items".

a person has an unspent conviction if
    the convictions of the person is a list
    and a conviction is in the list
    and it is not the case that the conviction is spent.

a person is eligible for the position if
    the age of the person is a number N
    and N >= 21
    and it is not the case that the person is bankrupt
    and it is not the case that the person has an unspent conviction.

the positive numbers is [1, 2, 3, 4, 5].

the mixed numbers is [-1, 2, -3, 4].

the empty list is [].

the single item is ["apple"].

the multiple items is ["apple", "banana", "cherry"].

